findings.body:
The PR description lists `flow-icon-text.test.tsx` ("Unit tests using MSW for API mocking") and the checklist marks "includes unit tests that cover the changes" as done. The diff and the head tree contain only `flow-icon-text.stories.tsx`, `flow-icon-text.tsx`, and `index.ts`. Nothing exercises the query, the `Link` target, or the rendered name.

The sibling components have tests for exactly this pattern. `deployment-link.test.tsx` mocks `/deployments/:id` with `server.use(http.get(buildApiUrl(...)))` inside a memory-history router, and the flow detail components have `*.test.tsx` files too. A test here would be cheap to write and would catch regressions in the query wiring or the link's `params`.

::code{file="ui-v2/src/components/flows/flow-icon-text/flow-icon-text.tsx" lines="20-32"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The checklist claim is false as submitted. Either add the test file or uncheck the box and drop the description line.

In `createTestRouter`, the router is given `context: { queryClient: new QueryClient() }`, but that client is never used. `FlowIconText` reads data through `useSuspenseQuery`, which uses the client from `QueryClientProvider`, which is the module-level `queryClient` in the decorator. The second client is dead weight, and it is also a new instance on every decorator render, which can mislead someone reading the story about where the data comes from.

The story also wraps `FlowIconText` in its own `<Suspense fallback>` (line 23), but the component already contains a `Suspense` boundary, so the outer one never triggers. Removing both makes the story reflect the real component contract.

::code{file="ui-v2/src/components/flows/flow-icon-text/flow-icon-text.stories.tsx" lines="20-34"}
